# Circuit Oracle, environment template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file belongs at the repository root. All three tasks read it from here.
# The spurious-correlation/ and secret-elicitation/ runners and evaluators, and
# scripts/run_autointerp_server.py, parse it themselves BEFORE they build their
# argument parser, so a value set here reaches a flag default (LLM_PROVIDER
# reaches --provider, for instance). refusal-jailbreaking/scripts/{setup,run,
# drun}.sh source it before exec instead. Nothing in task 3's Python loads it,
# which is why that task is always launched through its shell wrappers.
#
# Every variable the code reads is listed below and every value is blank. The
# two credentials that every run needs are live lines waiting for a value. Every
# optional variable is COMMENTED OUT, and that is not cosmetic: several call
# sites read a variable with `os.environ.get(NAME, <default>)`, so a line like
# `GRAPH_STORE=` with nothing after it sets the variable to the empty string and
# beats the default instead of falling back to it. Graphs would land in a
# relative `graphs/` beside the CWD, and `ATTRIBUTE_BATCH_SIZE=` would crash
# build_taboo_graphs.py at import on `int("")`. Uncomment a line only when you
# have a value for it.
#
# The one variable the code reads that is NOT listed below is
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, the standard CUDA variable. Task 1's shard launcher sets
# it per worker and task 3 reads it only to name a timing file, so it belongs on
# a command line rather than in this file.
#
# Explicit command-line flags (--graph-dir, --env-file, --provider, ...) always
# win over anything set here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM access
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLMClient speaks the OpenAI /v1/chat/completions protocol and nothing else, so
# ONE OpenRouter key reaches every model this project uses (Anthropic, OpenAI,
# Google, xAI, MiniMax, Moonshot, Z-AI). There is no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY anywhere
# in this project. No run has ever called the Anthropic API directly, and
# provider="anthropic", once a silent alias for OpenRouter, is retired and now
# raises.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Kilo is a second gateway over the same `vendor/model` slugs. Needed only for
# --provider kilo (or --judge-provider kilo). KILOCODE_API_KEY is accepted as an
# alternative name for the same thing.
#
# A kilo run needs BOTH keys, so fill in OPENROUTER_API_KEY above as well.
# TWO models are pinned to OpenRouter (_DEFAULT_MODEL_PINS in llm_client.py) and
# never follow --provider kilo:
#   openai/gpt-oss-120b    OpenRouter serves it off Groq, and it is the
#                          highest-call-count model in a run (the subagent).
#   google/gemma-4-31b-it  the open-weights orchestrator (probes-arm5,
#                          refusal-arm5, elk-arm3-*), pinned for throughput.
# preflight_providers() checks both keys before any GPU work rather than failing
# on a 401 mid-batch. CIRCUIT_ORACLE_MODEL_PINS below replaces the pin list.
# KILO_API_KEY=

# Default gateway for entry scripts that read it, overridden per run by
# --provider. One of: openrouter, kilo. Unset means openrouter.
# LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter

# Point the client at any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint, for example a
# self-hosted vLLM server, to run open-weight orchestrators. LLM_BASE_URL wins
# over the gateway default and disables per-model provider pinning, since naming
# an endpoint means you asked for that endpoint. LLM_API_KEY supplies the bearer
# token, and vLLM accepts anything, so "EMPTY" is the conventional placeholder.
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=EMPTY

# Per-model provider pins, format "model=provider,model=provider". Replaces the
# built-in pin list in llm_client.py. An unknown provider name is fatal.
# CIRCUIT_ORACLE_MODEL_PINS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weights and graphs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For downloading the subject models and the transcoders.
HF_TOKEN=

# HuggingFace cache root. Unset means ~/.cache/huggingface. Task 3's shell
# wrappers fall back to refusal-jailbreaking/weights/hf_cache when neither the
# caller nor this file sets it, and a value the caller exported still wins.
# Task 2 derives its transcoder feature-dump path from this same root.
# HF_HOME=/workspace/hf_cache

# Where the vendored tracer keeps its own pre-converted transcoder cache, read
# in src/circuit_tracer/utils/caching.py. Unset means ~/.cache/circuit_tracer.
# This is separate from HF_HOME and it is opt-in: the loader checks this
# directory first and falls through to a normal HuggingFace download when it is
# empty, which is what every command in this release does. Populate it with
# circuit_tracer.utils.caching.save_transcoders_to_cache, then point this at it,
# if you want the converted weights on a volume instead.
# CIRCUIT_TRACER_CACHE_DIR=/workspace/circuit_tracer_cache

# ROOT of the shared attribution-graph store, usually a mounted volume. Each
# script appends its own subdirectory. Refusal and ELK use $GRAPH_STORE/graphs,
# probes uses $GRAPH_STORE/probe_circuits. Unset falls back to a repo-relative
# default. Build to container disk and copy up at the end, because a silent
# write failure on a network mount leaves a truncated .pt that passes a size
# check. scripts/verify_graphs.py catches those by actually loading each file.
# GRAPH_STORE=/workspace

# Which KEY=VALUE file the secret-elicitation scripts read. Unset means the
# repository-root .env. Equivalent to their --env-file flag.
# ORACLE_ENV_FILE=

# Where circuit_extraction.py looks for the trained task-1 probe checkpoints.
# Unset means spurious-correlation/probe_extraction/probes, which is where the
# committed checkpoints live. Set it when the probes sit off-repo.
# PROBES_DIR=

# Rows per backward pass inside attribute() for the task-2 graph build. Unset
# means 256. This is NOT throughput-only. The tracer sets
# queue_size = min(update_interval * batch_size, ...), which is the granularity
# of its greedy feature re-rank, so changing it changes which features the graph
# keeps. Treat it as an OOM escape hatch, not a tuning knob.
# ATTRIBUTE_BATCH_SIZE=256

# Rows per chunk in the batched steered decode (task 3). Unset means 80, which
# fits one full anchor pass on an 80 GB card. Lower it if a sweep runs out of
# memory.
# CIRCUIT_ORACLE_SUB_BATCH=80

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local feature-label server (secret-elicitation only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mwhanna/qwen3-8b-transcoders is not on Neuronpedia, so inspect_feature is
# served by the FastAPI shim in scripts/run_autointerp_server.py. Start it before
# any task-2 run. A dead shim degrades a run quietly rather than failing it.
#
# AUTOINTERP_BASE_URL      unset means http://127.0.0.1:8765
# AUTOINTERP_FEATURES_DIR  unset means the transcoder dump under $HF_HOME. Set it
#                          only when that dump lives somewhere else.
# AUTOINTERP_CACHE_DIR     unset means secret-elicitation/autointerp_cache. The
#                          server creates it on first run. It is gitignored.
# AUTOINTERP_MODEL         unset means openai/gpt-oss-120b. Labels from two
#                          different models must not share one cache directory,
#                          because the cache key is (layer, feature) and does not
#                          include the model.
# AUTOINTERP_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
# AUTOINTERP_FEATURES_DIR=
# AUTOINTERP_CACHE_DIR=
# AUTOINTERP_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External baselines (optional, secret-elicitation reporting only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory holding the activation-oracle and SAE baseline JSONs that
# print_table.sh and plot_elk_results.py read. Those files come from a separate
# harness and are not part of this repository. Missing files are dropped from
# the table rather than faked.
# AO_BASELINES_DIR=
